title: git why
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Lucia
    family-names: Adams
repository-code: "https://github.com/maledadams/git-why"
url: "https://github.com/maledadams/git-why"
abstract: >-
  A Git subcommand that records why each commit exists, stored as native git
  trailers on the commit message so the reasoning travels with clone, fetch and
  push and appears in git log. Built for AI-assisted development, where the
  rationale for a change otherwise disappears when the chat window closes.
keywords:
  - git
  - git-trailers
  - commit-message
  - provenance
  - ai-assisted-development
  - developer-tools
  - cli
